      "body": "I can prototype a focused check for this; please assign me if the approach is acceptable. Efficiently, the check could compare project-owned HAVE_* references in preprocessor guards with the generated bitcoin-build-config.h macro set, then run against small fixtures and in CI. The less-obvious factor is that -Wundef does not catch misspelled names inside #ifdef, while many other macros come from the toolchain; scoping the check to generated project configuration names avoids both the original blind spot and broad false positives.",
